contentText:
Usher kicked a woman off stage during an uncomfortable interaction over the weekend, and now, she has issued a response clapping back at critics.&nbsp;

The singer brought the fan on stage for his performance of “Can U Handle It?” at the Saturday (July 25) stop of his and Chris Brown’s R&B Tour in Nashville. However, the steamy performance of the Confessions track turned into an awkward moment, as she didn’t appear to be feeling what was transpiring.

The exchange has since gone viral on social media, and the woman, who goes by Gabrielle Cheyenne on Facebook, fired back at those dissing her, according to Complex .

&#8220;First off NOBODY is declining to go on stage. I looked good asf, you thought I wasn&#8217;t gonna let THOUSANDS of people see me?? On the big screen, where you b—-es will never be???? My mom and I had FLOOR SEATS,” the woman wrote. “Their team approached us and moved us to VIP before the show even started !! PRETTY PRIVILEGES something you hoes will never know about!!”&nbsp;&nbsp;

She continued: “They don&#8217;t say who you&#8217;re going up there for!! Y&#8217;all wanted me to get up there and f–k him atp ?? CHATT FOLKS AREN&#8217;T USED TO ANYTHING. That&#8217;s the most exciting thing that would&#8217;ve happened in y&#8217;all little ass lives !! F–k yall, DISRESPECTFULLY.&#8221;&nbsp;

Livebitez captured a video comment from Gabrielle Cheyenne claiming she was hoping to be brought on stage for Chris Brown’s set, and not by Usher.

“Yes I want on stage and no they don’t tell you who, what, when, where. Baby, I wasn’t going up there for Usher, I wanted CHRIS and CHRIS only,” she claimed. “Anywayss, anybody who wasn’t sitting VIP or has a face card that doesn’t qualify should hush.”

An interview with the fan found her explaining that she wouldn’t change anything and that she didn’t feel “embarrassed” or “ruined” by the sour seranade. “There was even people harassing me as I was walking out of the stadium,” she said.

Billboard has reached out to Usher for comment.

Usher has yet to publicly address the matter after his Saturday performance. After kicking off in June, Brown and Usher’s R&B Tour will continue on Tuesday (July 28) with a show in Birmingham, Ala., before heading to Syracuse, N.Y., on Aug. 1.
